--swiftversion 6.2
--indent 2
--maxwidth 120
--linebreaks lf
--trimwhitespace always
--commas inline
--operatorfunc spaced
--ranges spaced
--semicolons never
--self remove
--patternlet hoist
--header ignore
# noForceUnwrapInTests rewrites `as!` into `try #require(... as?)`, which is a SEMANTIC change, not a
# formatting one. On CoreFoundation types the result does not compile: `dp as? CFBoolean` is a
# conditional downcast the compiler knows always succeeds, which is an error, so the sweep broke
# KeychainTests.swift. It also contradicts this repo's own stated policy -- .swiftlint.yml sets
# force_unwrapping to error with the note "Force unwrap is BANNED -- try! and as! allowed in tests
# only", i.e. `as!` in a test is deliberate and permitted. Disabled rather than worked around, and
# the two rewritten sites were restored to their original `as!` (Phase 10 / D-18).
--disable noForceUnwrapInTests
--exclude .build,Packages/.build,Packages/CortexCore/.build,Packages/CortexIPC/.build,Packages/CortexRender/.build,Packages/CortexDecoder/.build,Packages/CortexRing/.build,DerivedData,Cortex.xcodeproj,Cortex.xcworkspace,vendor,fastlane/Fastfile,fastlane/Matchfile,fastlane/Appfile
